    "long_instructions": "# Headings\r\n\r\nSo far, you've organized your content into paragraphs.  Another way HTML allows you to organize your code is by using **headings**.  A heading is a short piece of text that goes at the top of a section of content, like a title.\r\n\r\n# Do This:\r\n\r\n1) Find the headings in the web page below and use AI Tutor to learn about the code that makes them.\r\n2) Make sure you and your partner agree on what the tags do.\r\n3) Change the code so that \"Drawing\" and \"2 years\" match the headings on the rest of the page.\r\n\r\n::: details [🔎 **Show Me How** 🔍]\r\n\r\n![Gif showing how to change the headings](https://images.code.org/8c10b4b144e03116f480c0faade30dde-image-1767508634646.gif)\r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [**Help and Tips**]\r\n- [<i class=\"fa-regular fa-map\"></i> Headings and Paragraphs](https://levelbuilder-studio.code.org/courses/csd-2024/guides/headings-and-paragraphs)\r\n- [<i class=\"fa-solid fa-book\"></i> HTML Tags](https://levelbuilder-studio.code.org/courses/csd-2024/guides/html-tags)\r\n:::",
